    "background_story": "Quentin was a brilliant and eccentric musician who had a passion for obscure instruments. Among his vast collection, one instrument stood out - the heckelphone. This rare, double-reed woodwind instrument was Quentin's pride and joy. He spent years mastering its unique sound and nuances, often incorporating it into his compositions. As a member of a renowned avant-garde orchestra, Quentin's heckelphone playing added an otherworldly dimension to their performances. Critics raved about his ability to coax haunting, ethereal sounds from the instrument. Quentin's love for the heckelphone led him to become one of the world's leading authorities on the subject, and he traveled the globe to share his knowledge and showcase the instrument's beauty.",
